## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table shows how the source support ticket was originally grouped. The GitHub tracking issues below record each cause's engineering outcome.

## Fixed · shared parser

The shared parser read dates month first. For tenants whose locale writes the day first, it flipped the month and day before the booking was sent. Engineering fixed this with <code>fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales</code>.

**Tracking:** [Shared date parser issue #1 · closed as fixed](https://github.com/devduel/megadev-challenge/issues/1) · **379 reports**

## Won't fix · booking-v3 date hint

The booking-v3 form told people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY`, while the affected tenants use day-first dates. The form interpreted the entered value in the tenant's locale, reversing the date. Engineering retired the booking-v3 form, so it will not be fixed.

**Tracking:** [booking-v3 date hint issue #2 · closed as won't fix](https://github.com/devduel/megadev-challenge/issues/2) · **33 reports**

## Triage evidence

`meta.intakeTag` is an intake guess based on the reporter's browser locale, not proof of cause. Group by the tenant's configured locale and booking form, together with the report channel. The five reports noted as a one-day move still fall under the parser cause; they are not a third bug.

